	(text "Power filtering"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "222933c0-2e67-4593-9a10-cfe3492b78ac")
	)
	(text "Input RC low-pass filter with -3 dB point set around 150 kHz.\nSuppressing switching peaks."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2e25f7c4-639b-4e98-b7eb-3530068274ad")
	)
	(text "Output signal conditioning"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 29.21 134.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "60120b44-54a3-4231-80d2-eb876e039533")
	)
	(text "Transceiver"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 232.41 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7ce2b38e-24f9-4891-b509-b6eb00d3cb05")
	)
	(text "Output transistors Q104 (P-channel) and Q105 (N-channel) form a half-bridge configuration.\nCombined with inductor L101 and the parasitic capacitance of transceiver ST101, this circuit\nfunctions as a resonant driver.\nTransistor Q101 serves as a level shifter for the P-channel transistor Q104, which requires\nhigh-side switching. A voltage divider with an optional Zener diode prevents Vgs from exceeding\nits maximum rating.\nTransistor Q102 acts as a signal inverter for the N-channel transistor Q105.\nTransistor Q103 can disable Q105 by forcing it closed. When combined with a LOW signal on PWM,\nthis closes both half-bridge transistors, placing the SONIC signal in a high-impedance state\nto prevent interference with the received signal."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.84 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8b0dad93-91b0-4c73-aabe-56d678a7cc2d")
	)
	(text "Common source voltage filtering for both 3V3 and 24V voltage branches.\nPlace all capacitors close to transistors."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 88.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9c220e68-705b-4bbf-a176-c8d8a97450bb")
	)
	(text "The component must be an actual\ntransceiver capable of handling\nboth transmit and receive operations.\nA ground resistor enables current\nmeasurement and power calculations\nfor design evaluation."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 232.41 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a05d889c-4978-4193-9143-7f5e31f9d3cf")
	)
	(text "PWM signal filterring"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d7b005e6-a46b-4035-ab22-5e03ed4ad85f")
	)
	(text "Transceiver driver"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.84 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dba52eb1-7bf5-47c2-b0a8-e3ef776618ae")
	)
	(text "Two diodes limit the output voltage to ±0.7 V, protecting the output circuits from high-voltage peaks generated by the driver.\nA 100 kΩ resistor limits the current to prevent reducing the driver's power. This configuration constrains the bias voltage\ndivider, which requires a much higher resistance value to avoid attenuating the received signal."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 29.21 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f9b368b5-cafd-4fd6-8fe9-82fa21d49ccb")
	)
